  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "Rolf Mowatt-Larssen, a former officer of the CIA, the US foreign intelligence agency, says that in 2003, before the US invaded Iraq, he briefed President George W. Bush in the Oval Office, with CIA director George Tenet. He says he told the president, \"We know where he is,\" meaning Abu Musab al-Zarqawi, a man the US was hunting, who he says was in a camp in northeast Iraq. He tells it as an inside view of the decisions made just before the war."
}
